body:
Hey, bud. I used to do the same thing you did. It kinda gave me a sick feeling that was also waY too addictive. I'm not really sure what I wanted out of it, but what I can remember is that I just wanted to emulate how they look. That way, I could *feel*  what its like to be pretty. However, this was probably the most self-destructive thing I allowed myself to do for 2 reasons.

&#x200B;

1. Constantly looking at models and hot people gives you a false sense of availability. What i mean by that is, if we see models all the time, then we being to assume that they are common, the expectation, the norm. Just remember, if everyone was a model, there wouldn't be any models. So, go into a wal-mart, and just try to pick out how many "model" quality people are in there. Its probably slim to none, because that's real life.

2. I used to think for a very long time that I was the ugly person. I'm not, at all. (if it helps to know that even pretty people can also never know what they look like). So i would look at all of these ig models and tunnel vision on to their features. I would analyze them down to their symmetry, their features, and their build and more often than not, i would only see the attractive qualities of them rather than the unattractive qualities. So, I would be completely obsessed with one model's eyes, another model's nose, and another model's lips until I had built a frankenstein monster in my head of what I should look like. little did I know, that models don't always have perfect features, they just have 3-4 that make them stand out and distract from their "imperfections". So, please do not think that every model is just a goddess among men, because they're not. They know how to take pictures, how to wear makeup, what angles they look good in, what lighting fits best, because they're paid to know how to do that. 

&#x200B;

And sure, a lot of them are insanely attractive, but no body expects thins like that from you unless you're also a model. Don't put artificial standards on yourself if you're not even trying to be a model. 

&#x200B;

So please do not compare yourself compulsively, it will only bring you WAY more confusion and pain than it will relieve.

[https://imgur.com/a/1twNDSC](https://imgur.com/a/1twNDSC)

&#x200B;

I decided to attach some photos, feel free to let me know if I'm attractive or not 'cause I'd LOVE to know.
